{"toolCallId":"call_55f9f5796c604cb5a3375b3212217936","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"\nSpec Folder Validation v3.0.0\n\n  Folder: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent\n  Level:  1\n  Engine: orchestrator\n\n+ FILE_EXISTS: All required files present for Level 1\n! PLACEHOLDER_FILLED: 37 unfilled value token(s) in a Draft packet. Fill each one before the status leaves Draft\n    - spec.md:3: description: \"[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain poin\n    - spec.md:23: | **Priority** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: P0/P1/P2] |\n    - spec.md:36: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\n    - spec.md:39: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: One-sentence outcome statement. What does success look like?]\n    - spec.md:57: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 1]\n    - spec.md:58: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 2]\n    - spec.md:59: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 3]\n    - spec.md:62: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 1] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n    - spec.md:63: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 2] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n    - spec.md:69: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: path/to/file.js] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Modify/Create/Delete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description] |\n    - spec.md:83: | REQ-001 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to verify it's done] |\n    - spec.md:89: | REQ-002 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to verify it's done] |\n    - spec.md:98: - **SC-001**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Primary measurable outcome]\n    - spec.md:99: - **SC-002**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Secondary measurable outcome]\n    - spec.md:110: | Dependency | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/API] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What if blocked] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Fallback plan] |\n    - spec.md:111: | Risk | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Risk description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: High/Med/Low] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Mitigation strategy] \n    - spec.md:120: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Question 1 requiring clarification]\n    - spec.md:121: - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Question 2 requiring clarification]\n    - plan.md:24: | **Language/Stack** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n    - plan.md:25: | **Framework** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n    - plan.md:26: | **Storage** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n    - plan.md:27: | **Testing** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n    - plan.md:46: - [ ] [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: The test command and the output it must print]\n    - plan.md:57: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n    - plan.md:60: - **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n    - plan.md:61: - **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n    - plan.md:64: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n    - tasks.md:47: - [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]\n    - tasks.md:48: - [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]\n    - tasks.md:49: - [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]\n    - tasks.md:50: - [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]\n    - implementation-summary.md:50: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Opening hook: 2-3 sentences on what changed and why it matters. Lead with impact.]\n    - implementation-summary.md:61: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: path] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Created/Modified/Deleted] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What this change accomplishe\n    - implementation-summary.md:70: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How was this tested, verified and shipped? What was the rollout approach?]\n    - implementation-summary.md:81: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What was decided] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Active-voice rationale with specific reasoning] |\n    - implementation-summary.md:92: | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Validation, lint, tests, manual check] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: PASS/FAIL with specifics] |\n    - implementation-summary.md:101: 1. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Limitation]** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Specific detail with workaround if one exists.]\n+ TEMPLATE_SOURCE: Template source headers present\n+ ANCHORS_VALID: Anchors well formed in 4 file(s)\n+ FRONTMATTER_VALID: Frontmatter continuity basics present\n+ FRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK: All spec-doc frontmatter memory blocks are structurally valid\n+ SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY: All targeted spec-doc anchors meet the sufficiency baseline\n+ MERGE_LEGALITY: No merge plan supplied; legality check skipped\n+ CROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION: No routing payload supplied; contamination check skipped\n+ POST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT: No post-save payload supplied; fingerprint check skipped\n+ GRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT: Graph metadata checked\n+ GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY: Generated metadata passed schema, status-enum and path-prefix invariants\n+ GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT: Generated synopsis fields match the current docs\n+ COMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER: No ephemeral comment-hygiene markers found\n+ SCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED: Spec status is 'Draft', not Complete; scaffold markers are allowed\n+ STATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY: status cross-doc check not applicable; one status is missing or unclassified\n    - spec.md Status=Draft classified=planned\n    - implementation-summary.md Status=<missing> classified=unknown\n+ AC_COVERAGE: Acceptance coverage gate not active for this level or lifecycle state\n+ AC_CLOSURE: Acceptance closure gate not active below Level 2\n+ TOC_POLICY: TOC policy passed: no TOC headings in non-research spec documents\n+ AI_PROTOCOLS: AI protocol check not applicable for Level 1\n+ COMPLEXITY_MATCH: Complexity level consistent with content (Level 1; phases=3, tasks=13, stories=0, scenarios=0)\n+ FOLDER_NAMING: Folder name '001-completeness-min-percent' follows naming convention\n+ FRONTMATTER_VALUES: Frontmatter